Currently there are two different shell scripts for building the docs (build_and_deploy_docs.sh and fast_build_docs.sh). These can be changed from bash scripts to Python scripts. In addition there should be an option for building the docs but not deploying them, therefore a third script.
@MarcoGorelli do you think it might be better to have just a single Python script, where arguments are passed upon execution, instead of having three separate scripts? So someone can do build_script.py --mode=fast?
I can start working on this.
